{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile is the strongest tested direction (config_005/006, ~0.65 accuracy and ~0.63 F1), while image-only ResNet50 is weak (config_011, ~0.33 accuracy). The key uncertainty is whether adding image information to the best RNA representation provides complementary signal. config_030 keeps the RNA side identical to the strong config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and adds only ResNet50 with simple concat fusion, matching the already tested image-only ResNet50 setting. This isolates the effect of multimodal fusion rather than changing aggregation or image encoder, making it the most informative next experiment under a limited budget."
}

